=== ISSUE.md
     1	# INC-5521: Oversold stock and stuck holds during the September flash sale
     2	
     3	Reported by the checkout team after the 2026-09-12 flash sale.
     4	
     5	## What we saw
     6	
     7	- The `sneaker-limited` drop had 250 units. We confirmed 263 orders, and 13
     8	  customers had to be refunded.
     9	- The stock dashboard showed `reserved` going negative for two SKUs after the
    10	  sale, and it has not recovered.
    11	- Some customers who retried checkout after a timeout had units held twice for
    12	  one order; the second hold only disappeared when the reservation expired.
    13	- One order was rejected because a bundle item was out of stock, but the other
    14	  item in the bundle stayed held until we restarted the worker pool.
    15	- Finance reports `sold` counts that are higher than the number of orders we
    16	  shipped for a few SKUs.
    17	
    18	## Context
    19	
    20	Every checkout worker calls `InventoryService` concurrently. During the sale
    21	we ran 40 workers. The nightly `expire()` job ran once during the sale.
    22	
    23	The unit tests all pass, and none of this reproduces when we click through
    24	checkout by hand.
    25	
    26	A service-wide lock (INC-5490) stopped the overselling in staging but cut
    27	checkout throughput by 90% and was rolled back the same day.
